120.steps:
1. Prepare 3 routers, sonicwall 1, sonicwall 2 , router 1, sonicwall 2 acts as ABR,it must advertise a default route into the stub area via summary-LSAs;;
2. Configure sonicwall 2 interface X5, zone LAN, static IP 5.5.5.1, connect to sonicwall 1 X5, sonicwall 1 X5 has static IP 5.5.5.5, enable OSPF on sonicwall 1 X5 and sonicwall 2 X5,area 2, area type: Stub Area;
3. Configure sonicwall 2 interface X3, zone LAN, static IP 28.1.1.46, connect to router 1, router 1 has static ip 28.1.1.28, enable OSPF on them , area 0, area type: Normal ;
4. Use command "redistribute static subnets" on router 1, to redistribute the static route on router 1, and router 1 has static route 20.1.1.0/24;
5. Check the OSPF status of sonicwall 1, sonicwall 2 and router 1, all the status change from Loading to FULL;
6. Use command "show ip ospf database external" on sonicwall 2, check the external LSA, it has received Type5 LSAs from router 1;
7. Use command "show ip ospf database external" on sonicwall 1, check the external LSA, there's no Type5 LSAs on Sonicwall 1.
8. Use command "show ip ospf database summary" to check if sonicwall 2 has correct behavior as a stub area ABR, it must advertise a default route to all routers belongs to this stub area.

