114.steps:
1. Configure interface X3 in sonicwall, zone LAN, static IP address 28.1.1.46, connect to router, router has static IP 28.1.1.28;
2. Configure interface X2 in sonicwall, zone LAN, static IP address 20.1.1.20/24;
3. Enable OSPF in X3 in sonicwall, enable OSPF on router, area 0, enable redistribute connected network in sonicwall;
4. Wait and check sonicwall and router can reach FULL state;
5. Use command "show ip ospf database external" in router, see router could learn route 20.1.1.0/24 from sonicwall;
6. Shutdown interface X2 in sonicwall, check the neighbor router's external database, the database has been updated, the route 20.1.1.0/24 was disappeared;
7. Link UP interface X2 in sonicwall, check the neighbor router's external database, the database has been updated, the route 20.1.1.0/24 appeared;
8. Change interface X2's ip subnet mask, change to 20.1.1.20/20, check the neighbor router's external database, the database has been updated, the route has been changed to 20.1.0.0/20.
9. Change interface X2's IP address to 200.1.1.1/24, check the neighbor router's external database, the database has been updated, the route has been changed to 200.1.1.0/24.

114.result:
in step 4, the OSPF status LED turns to GREEN.
In step 6, after the connected interface X2 is shutdown, the neighbor router will update its OSPF database, route 20.1.1.0/24 will disappear;
in step 7, after the connected interface X2 is link up, the neighbor router will update its OSPF database, route 20.1.1.0/24 will appear;
in step 8, after the connected interface X2's subnet mask was changed, the neighbor router will update its OSPF database, route 20.1.1.0/24 will change to 20.1.1.0/20.
in step 9, after the connected interface X2's ip address was changed, the new connected route will be advertised, route 200.1.1.0/24 will appear on neighbor router' s OSPF database.�

